# Campaign learning rule log

When you learn something new from maintainer review, CI, CLA, or a rework on an allowlisted DE PR:

1. **Log it first** with an append-only entry:
   ```bash
   oocoder campaign learn \
     --repo owner/name \
     --source '#PR' \
     --title 'short title' \
     --rule 'durable rule text' \
     --encode
   ```
   Or append the same shape under today's `## YYYY-MM-DD` in `docs/CAMPAIGN_RULE_LOG.md`.
2. **Roll up** the rule into the matching topic section in `docs/CAMPAIGN_LEARNINGS.md`.
3. **Encode** into `packages/core/src/implement.ts` when future patches should follow it (titles, CLA, allocsize, Sphinx headings, etc.).
4. Do not silently "just remember" a learning in chat — if it should change the next PR, it belongs in the rule log.

Skip one-off typos that will not recur. Prefer conservative, repo-specific rules.
